#paths every machine checks out at bootstrap, whatever it already carries.
#One per line, relative to $HOME, leading slash optional. A line whose first
#non-blank character is # is a comment.
#
#dot reads this out of the repository itself (git show HEAD:.dot/include),
#before anything is in the work tree, so adding a file to every machine is a
#commit here and not a new version of ~/.bin/dot. Everything else stays in
#the repository until 'dot get /<path>' asks for it.
#
#A repository without this file still bootstraps: dot falls back to
#.gitignore and .bin/dot, which is the least a machine needs to fetch the
#rest. Keep that pair listed here anyway - the fallback is a floor, not a
#default.

.gitignore
.bin/dot

#this file, so a machine can read and edit the list it was built from
.dot/include

#Claude Code's instructions. CLAUDE.md imports RTK.md and points at
#parallel-sessions.md, so the three only make sense together
.claude/CLAUDE.md
.claude/RTK.md
.claude/parallel-sessions.md

#the directories wcd's index must never learn: caches, build trees and
#version-control internals. Without it the first nightly rebuild on a new
#machine walks every node_modules it can reach
.ban.wcd
